<title>UK: Rentokil off as broker says &quot;take profits&quot;.</title>
<headline>Rentokil off as broker says &quot;take profits&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Rentokil Initial Plc dipped on Thursday as the broad market firmed after brokerage SBC Warburg told its clients to take profits, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1058 GMT, the shares were down 8p to 481, as the FTSE 100 looked set to climb to a fresh record high.</p>
<p>Dealers said Warburg recommended clients take profits because the stock had reached its target of 480p.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
